1. DONE - col.inactive_border / col.active_border now follow pywal. The colours
   come from ~/.cache/wal/colors-hyprland.conf, which waypaper's hook generates
   on every wallpaper change using the SAME accent-scoring Theme.qml uses, so
   the borders and the bar always agree. See wallpaper_update.sh.

2. Wallpapers live in ~/Pictures/Wallpapers (waypaper's configured folder) and
   it is currently empty - put some images there before first login, or the
   palette never gets generated and everything falls back to Catppuccin.

3. Untested on real hardware: the four `global` binds that dispatch to the bar
   (screenshot x2, clipboard, keep-awake). They depend on quickshell having
   registered appid "quickshell"; if a key does nothing, check `hyprctl binds`
   and the bar's log - a name mismatch fails silently on both sides.
